 professional who can assess if there is an underlying issue.\n\nUnderstanding that these situations are challenging, remember that your frustration is understandable. It might help to try and approach each situation with empathy. For your son, try to be patient and perhaps work on memory strategies together. For instance, encourage note-taking, verbal repetition, or using visual aids. For your grandfather, you might consider having a conversation about his routine and what support he might need.\n\nIt might also be beneficial to seek support from family members or professionals. Sometimes a family meeting can help everyone understand the challenges and work together on solutions.\n\nI hope that helps. Let me know if you need more specific advice or support strategies."}
